<section>
  <h2>Code options: alignment</h2>

  <p>
    Alignment: <c>halign=</c> and <c>valign=</c> (<c>start</c> | <c>center</c> | <c>end</c>), or the classes <c>left</c> <c>center</c> <c>right</c> and <c>top</c> <c>middle</c> <c>bottom</c> in <c>class=</c>.
    Without them the code follows its slide: <c>start</c>, unless the slide says otherwise.
    Other options: <c>id</c> (the animation), classes <c>lines</c> and <c>panel</c>, <c>title=</c>, <c>size=</c>, <c>fit=none</c>, <c>focus=</c>, <c>transition=</c> (see the next slides).
  </p>
  <code lang=typescript id=g1 class=left>
    <frame>
      const where = "left";
    </frame>
    <frame>
      const where = "still left, now longer";
    </frame>
  </code>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Code options: size</h2>

  <p>
    <c>size=14</c> fixes the font size in pixels. Without it the code is scaled to fit,
    using the largest frame of the section, so the size never jumps between frames.
  </p>
  <code lang=typescript id=g2 size=14>
    <frame>
      const small = "size=14";
    </frame>
    <frame>
      const small = "size=14, and the same font size in every frame";
    </frame>
  </code>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Code options: <c>class="right top"</c></h2>
  <code lang=typescript class="right top">
    const corner = "top right";
  </code>
</section>

<notes>
  Options are attributes of the tag: <code lang=ts class=left size=18>
</notes>

<notes>
  Next: focus=, fit and size in detail.
</notes>
